 "poem": "I thought I had seen the darkness\nThrough some small window of darkness,\nBut was startled by darkness\nI could not see--or hardly\nSee, though I saw it never!\nOh! let my shadow disappear!\nAnd feel no twilight, darkness,\nOr light or darkness reappear\nBefore your eyes. alas!\nNo, no; the tower tower\nIn which you dwell upon heaven.\nThe stars were still before",
